    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vŏlūcra</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		volvo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a kind of worm</i> or <i>caterpillar that wraps
				itself up in vineleaves</i> (called also convolvulus), <i><span class="en">Col. Arb.
				15</span></i>.—It is also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vŏlūcre</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 17,
				28, 47, § 265</span></i>; and plur.
			volucres, <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 333</span></i>.</div>
